Teach libtool's `host_os` cases in configure about substrate.

mpg123 ships its configure pre-generated.  Libtool's `host_os` case
statements don't list `substrate*`, so when --host=i386-unknown-
substrate is passed:

  * `lt_cv_deplibs_check_method` falls through to "unknown" (no
    pattern), so libtool can't decide which files are shared libs.
  * `lt_prog_compiler_pic` is left empty, so PIC builds use no flag.
  * The shared-link `archive_cmds` block leaves `ld_shlibs=no`.
  * The dynamic-linker-properties block falls through to the catch-
    all `*)` arm, which sets `dynamic_linker=no` and therefore
    `can_build_shared=no`.

End result: configure prints "checking if libtool supports shared
libraries... no" and the build silently falls back to static-only,
even though substrate has libdl + ld.so Phase 4e
(dlopen/dlsym/dlclose).

substrate's ld.so is GNU/Linux-compatible (SONAME-based ELF,
LD_LIBRARY_PATH, /lib + /usr/lib search paths, -fPIC PIC model), so
the simplest correct fix is to alias `substrate*` into each of the
four GNU/ELF case matches in the shipped configure.

We patch the generated configure rather than m4/libtool.m4 because:
  * mpg123 ships configure pre-generated; no autoreconf is expected
    at consumer-side build time.
  * libtool.m4 has the same case match seven times across different
    sections; a fully comprehensive m4 patch is materially larger
    than the four configure edits and gains nothing unless someone
    re-runs autoreconf.  When that need arises, generate a
    companion patch from a fresh autoreconf diff.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -8949,7 +8949,7 @@ freebsd* | dragonfly* | midnightbsd*)
   ;;

 # This must be glibc/ELF.
-linux* | k*bsd*-gnu | kopensolaris*-gnu | gnu*)
+linux* | substrate* | k*bsd*-gnu | kopensolaris*-gnu | gnu*)
   lt_cv_deplibs_check_method=pass_all
   ;;

@@ -12338,7 +12338,7 @@ case $host_os in
     # old Intel for x86_64, which still supported -KPIC.
       ;;

-    linux* | k*bsd*-gnu | kopensolaris*-gnu | gnu*)
+    linux* | substrate* | k*bsd*-gnu | kopensolaris*-gnu | gnu*)
       case $cc_basename in
       # old Intel for x86_64, which still supported -KPIC.
       ecc*)
@@ -13011,7 +13011,7 @@ _LT_EOF
       archive_expsym_cmds='sed "s|^|_|" $export_symbols >$output_objdir/$soname.expsym~$CC -shared $pic_flag $libobjs $deplibs $compiler_flags $wl-h,$soname $wl--retain-symbols-file,$output_objdir/$soname.expsym $wl--image-base,`expr ${RANDOM-$$} % 4096 / 2 \* 262144 + 1342177280` -o $lib'
       ;;

-    gnu* | linux* | tpf* | k*bsd*-gnu | kopensolaris*-gnu)
+    gnu* | linux* | substrate* | tpf* | k*bsd*-gnu | kopensolaris*-gnu)
       tmp_diet=no
       if test linux-dietlibc = "$host_os"; then
 	case $cc_basename in
@@ -14836,7 +14836,7 @@ android*)
   ;;

 # This must be glibc/ELF.
-linux* | k*bsd*-gnu | kopensolaris*-gnu | gnu*)
+linux* | substrate* | k*bsd*-gnu | kopensolaris*-gnu | gnu*)
   version_type=linux # correct to gnu/linux during the next big refactor
   need_lib_prefix=no
   need_version=no
